WEBVTT

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.690
<b>Drama Club</b>

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.970
<i>What's their problem?</i>

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.650
<i>Do they think they can tell us what to do?</i>

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.650
<i>Let's teach them a lesson.</i>

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.020
<i>That sounds fun.</i>

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.880
<b>Tenth Haunting 
School Ghost Stories?</b>

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:04.340
You know that tiny storeroom by the stage?

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.760
Normally, the Drama Club 
stores their props there.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.430
But every night, you can hear voices inside.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.030
When you enter,

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.200
they say it feels creepy, 
like someone's watching you!

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.050
How scary!

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:33.600
Why are you all surrounding 
me while you eat lunch?

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.410
Because your lunch looks so delicious!

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.910
It's so pretty and cute...

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.190
Can I take a photo?

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.510
You already did.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.890
It really is cute!

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:51.780
<i>Jeez! Others are watching, you know?</i>

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.020
<i>Sheesh.</i>

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.670
So what's this about ghosts?

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.230
Supposedly, it started this year.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.900
That's when the ghost story began to spread.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:02.730
Huh...

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.950
Maybe the ghost is a voyeur!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.540
Someone probably imagined it.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:13.070
And also, wouldn't a Drama Club 
member want to be seen?

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.750
That sounds like sexual harassment.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.000
You're gonna get sued Inaba-kun!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.010
Want a lawyer?

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.600
Shut up.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.250
I'm not interested in ghosts, anyway!

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.960
Master. Master...

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.350
Master.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.740
Did you hear a voice?

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.190
Nope! Nothing!

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.990
Definitely not a voice!

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.070
Are you hiding something?

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.270
How suspicious!

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:42.950
I-It's nothing at all...

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.260
Of course there's something!

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.640
Was it here? Did the weird 
voice come from here?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.920
What are you hiding from us?

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.110
Hey, where are you putting your hands?!

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.520
It's fine!

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.380
Come on, let me see!

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.680
You...

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.600
Stupid brats,

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.720
stop flirting with each other!

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.220
What was that?

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.190
"Flirting"?

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:29.470
Sure, we were being loud, 
but why was he so mad?

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.000
That's right.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.620
It's lunch break.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.780
What a creep.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:34.540
Hey...

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.780
What's "flirting"?

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.320
You're asking that?

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.080
Yes, what does "flirting" mean?

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.480
Well... It's when a boy and girl—

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.210
Enough.

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:49.390
Basically, it means you want sex—

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:50.390
Tashiro!

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.570
Huh? No way!

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.900
What the heck?!

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.730
Wait, that means Miura sees us that way?

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.180
That's kind of annoying!

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.830
Maybe we really should consider a lawsuit.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.090
We weren't flirting!

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:05.320
Jeez...

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:10.860
<i>But Miura sure was acting weird.</i>

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.760
No one's here, right?

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:28.450
Fool...

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:29.350
Yes, master!

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.090
I told you to stay put!

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.450
I'm so sorry, master...

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:39.480
I found the girls' conversation 
of extreme interest.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.830
What?

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.700
You believe in school ghost stories, too?

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.900
Indeed.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.400
How stupid.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.280
I haven't ever heard of suicides 
or accidents at this school.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:54.540
All the more reason you should 
use your power to investigate!

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.470
Why me?

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:58.360
If you find nothing, you find nothing.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:02.980
But if you find something, 
you have us to help you!

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.710
I get it. You're bored, right?

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.710
Let's start with some fortunetelling!

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.470
Fortunetelling? You can do that?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.220
Indeed! Leave it to us!

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.590
Here is the page.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:17.830
Go ahead, master!

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:19.640
Oh, fine...

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:22.230
Wheel of Fortune, Norns!

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.270
The Norns...

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:30.550
The three goddesses of fate: 
Skuld, Thandi, Urdr!

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:31.750
Goddesses?

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:36.430
You called, master?

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:38.480
Goddesses?

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.890
I-Is something wrong?

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:44.020
We tried to appear modern...

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.590
Where did you get that information?

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:47.960
Where?

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:49.090
Cait Sith.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.270
Are you stupid?

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:54.570
Don't believe that lying cat.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.920
I told you that I didn't want to do this!

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.560
What are you talking about?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.520
Of all the Petits, he's the most informed!

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.490
How?

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.640
He's making us wear these weird outfits!

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:08.010
You said you wanted to look modern, too!

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.420
So what's their deal?

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:13.200
Well, they don't get along so well...

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:17.900
I apologize that you had to see that, master.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:17.910
<b>Eldest: Skuld</b>

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:20.440
So, what are we fortunetelling?

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.710
<b>Second Eldest: Thandi</b>

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.510
It isn't my fault.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.500
<b>Youngest: Urdr</b>

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.620
Fine, tell me about the ghost 
stories of this school.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.540
Please leave it to us.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.140
The Norns use a wide variety of techniques.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:44.560
Fortunetelling, clairvoyance, 
and witchcraft, as well.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:49.160
When their hearts come together, 
their true power will be revealed!

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:52.500
I hate this outfit!

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.680
Don't say that now.

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.990
Hey, concentrate!

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:58.620
I can't concentrate with you like that!

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:58.610
Shut up, weirdo.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.620
I said to concentrate on the fortunetelling!

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:04.230
Why not call a weirdo a "weirdo"?

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.610
The Petits are really useless.

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:05.870
Hey, I see it.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.390
Learn anything?

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.060
Yes.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:18.630
Something... feels muddy.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:20.560
Huh?

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.390
Muddy.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.760
What's muddy?

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:30.360
Return.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:37.100
Okay, time for afternoon classes.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:42.300
Master, it seems something really is amiss.

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:44.530
Let us investigate for real!

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:45.790
No way...

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.320
Why not?

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.880
Even with what the Norns said?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.750
I can't believe in that.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.460
Don't say that.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:57.180
I am quite curious about Miura-sensei myself.

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:58.590
Miura, huh?

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:02.250
Are you not, master?

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:03.610
Well, I guess.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:07.860
I knew it! Something is 
definitely in this school!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:09.600
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:13.670
<i>Come to think of it, he's teaching 
English next period.</i>

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:16.030
<i>I wonder how mad he is.</i>

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.580
Listen, this is important.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:30.230
Hey, he's totally different than before.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:34.260
Yeah. I guess he's normal.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:37.890
But it's like lunchtime never happened.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:41.250
He was yelling so much.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:43.890
I feel like an idiot for being scared.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.380
I know.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.980
What are you planning?

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.500
Nothing...

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.610
I was just thinking that he 
was creeping me out,

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.760
so maybe I'll look into his background.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.240
Don't go too crazy.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.380
I'll tell you if I find anything, okay?

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:11.250
All right, master...

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.320
Time to start the investigation.

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:14.760
Investigation?

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:19.180
The muddy ghost story, you know.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.590
Oh... No, I have work today.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.680
Huh?!

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.450
But I was looking forward to it!

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:26.980
That isn't my problem.

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:31.590
<i>Miura?</i>

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.860
<i>What is he doing in the lecture hall?</i>

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.440
Hey, sexy boy...

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:53.970
Heading home alone?

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.710
Your friends aren't with you?

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:58.920
He's the one with all the girls?

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.430
He doesn't look that special to me.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.830
Lucky guy...

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.800
Share 'em with me. Even if you've 
already slept with them.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.140
Wh-What?

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:14.510
You wanna fight?

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:16.750
Don't get cocky!

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:22.240
D-Don't think you're so special!

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:26.050
What? You're jealous?

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.160
How stupid.

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:29.860
Shut up!

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:32.740
Fool, let's give them a scare.

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:33.820
What?!

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:39.420
Using the <i>Petit Hierozoicon</i> on 
lowlifes like these is a waste!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.520
Just do it.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.590
Very well...

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.790
Threaten them. Nothing more.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:48.680
What?

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.760
Judgment, Brondis!

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:53.270
Brondis!

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:57.900
The lightning that awakens the dead 
from Hell at the last judgment.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:06.190
Huh?

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:07.600
What was that sound?

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:08.690
An explosion?

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.310
C-Crap.

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:20.950
Ready...

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:22.230
Go!

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.970
Go! Go!

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:32.540
How did this happen to me?!

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:38.390
The Petits are so much fun, aren't they?

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.810
I didn't think it would be so loud.

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:44.070
It was like a tank's main gun.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.990
You say that like you've heard one.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:51.870
I have. Hase and I once went to 
see an SDF training exercise.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:01.300
It was probably a good lesson for those kids.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.980
Well, it's normal for boys that age to 
be jealous of popularity with girls.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:08.370
Being jealous is normal?

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:10.070
Yeah.

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.550
No matter how stupid they are,

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:17.090
showing your emotions when 
you're young is good.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.770
Or you'll eventually hit a dead end.

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:22.720
A dead end?

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.100
Yeah.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:27.900
Life's an endless series of 
small, stupid experiences.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:31.250
But if you can't learn from them,

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.700
you'll start refusing to 
interact with others.

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:38.510
And those people say the same 
thing: "It isn't my fault."

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.420
<i>Refusing to interact with others?</i>

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:43.760
Inaba's so gloomy.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.650
He doesn't seem to like others.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:49.200
<i>That's like my old self.</i>

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:55.230
<i>If I hadn't met Hase...</i>

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:59.980
<i>If I hadn't met the people here...</i>

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:03.610
<i>I wouldn't have talked to others 
or been able to believe in them.</i>

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:07.590
<i>I'd have cared only about my perspective,
 become a stupid adult,</i>

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:10.780
<i>and finally, ended up alone.</i>

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.240
<i>But it's different now.</i>

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.650
<i>I'm surrounded by other people, 
with other values,</i>

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:19.760
<i>experiencing things I'd have never imagined.</i>

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:23.340
<i>As what I once believed is 
constantly broken and remade.</i>

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:28.550
<i>And right now, that process 
makes me very happy.</i>

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:32.850
Ruriko-san, thanks!

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:35.190
You eat a lot, huh?

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:39.440
So communication is important, huh?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.640
That's right.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:43.370
No matter how small, 
even if it doesn't matter.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:46.960
As long as someone is there, 
words are important.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.440
Even if it's a pain, you talk.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:54.680
Making the extra effort 
is what leads to trust.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:59.140
Trust isn't something built up in a day.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.450
You can tell by looking 
at your friend, right?

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:02.950
That's right.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:06.350
Indeed, master!

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:10.010
Please stop summoning us for 
nonsense, as you did today.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:11.560
What was that?

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:13.590
No one said anything about that rule.

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:17.030
We would like you to aim higher.

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:21.530
Being used on lowlifes like that 
lowers our reputation... Hmph!

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.740
They really care for their master, huh?

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:27.920
I guess, as master of a magic 
book, you need to do better.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.720
But if I'm your master,

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:32.230
dealing with certain things is 
the most you can expect.

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:33.150
What?

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:36.280
Please aim higher.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.630
Don't expect too much of a high school boy!

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:41.660
"Dig deep where you stand,

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.830
and you're sure to find a spring."

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.040
Chogyu Takayama.

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:47.460
What?

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:52.250
If something is on your mind, 
keep at it as long as possible.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.010
That's one of youth's privileges.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.570
That's right.

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.020
Chirpity-chirp!

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.860
Huh? Looks like you aren't eating, chirp.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:05.460
Okay! We'll help, chirp.

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.350
I love glazed tofu, chirp!

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:09.600
Hey! Don't eat my food!

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:10.720
Chirp! Chirp!

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:26.500
At last, you are truly ready 
to investigate, master?

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:27.180
I guess.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.890
Splendid!

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:30.500
That's my master!

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:36.860
We are all looking forward to 
seeing you crack the case!

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:41.680
Hey, Fool, I've been wondering something.

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.900
What, exactly, do you want from me?

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.450
That is, of course...

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.660
You definitely wouldn't want me

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:51.270
to behave like the protagonist 
of a manga or a novel, right?

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:53.740
You do?!

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:55.470
Listen...

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:59.520
I'm not interested, and I don't 
have that kind of power.

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:02.080
He got all slippery.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.890
You must not assume that.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.910
The world is full of possibilities.

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:13.160
And perhaps dreams and 
adventure await you!

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:14.000
Shut up.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:16.200
My life's dream is...

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:17.920
to work for the prefectural government!

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:23.870
T-Tashiro?

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:26.890
You scared me! What is this?

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:30.220
Why are you talking about dreams 
of the future in the auditorium?

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.650
Shut up! I'm busy!

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:35.600
And what are you doing here, Tashiro?

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:37.180
What am I doing?

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:40.470
I said I was going to look 
into Miura, didn't I?

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.320
Yeah.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:45.250
Doesn't the Drama Club use that storeroom?

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:49.490
And Miura is the Drama Club 
adviser, you see...

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:50.320
Seriously?

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.540
Yeah. Well, the sub-adviser.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:57.840
There were rumors about how the Drama 
Club kids felt watched in here.

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.300
So I figured I should investigate.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:02.130
What's wrong?

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:03.130
Nothing.

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:05.280
Let's give it a look, I guess.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:06.050
Okay.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:16.280
<i>What is this place?</i>

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:18.370
<i>The air feels so heavy.</i>

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:19.870
<i>This feeling is...</i>

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:22.550
It smells so moldy in here!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.290
Master!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.970
It seems...

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:28.200
Yeah. Something is here.

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:32.380
Wigs, tape, and are those scripts?

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.800
I guess the Drama Club needs a lot of stuff.

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:38.430
<i>The walls are covered in stains and cracks.</i>

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:39.990
<i>This place is pretty old.</i>

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:43.150
What is this?

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:46.390
Why is cardboard stuck on here?

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:49.860
It's like it's hiding something.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:51.730
I'll rip it off.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:52.300
Okay.

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:04.660
What is this?

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:09.660
<i>It's all disgusting words 
used to curse women!</i>

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:19.130
<i>From this little window, 
you can see the auditorium.</i>

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.500
<i>Right...</i>

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:26.200
<i>Someone was watching girls practicing 
for clubs while they wrote this.</i>

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:31.850
<i>This is what the Norns were talking about.</i>

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.510
<i>It's like disgusting mud!</i>

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:36.350
I feel sick...

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:37.400
Tashiro?

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:41.760
Hey, did Miura write this?

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:42.780
I don't know.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:46.740
See how the ink is thinner here?

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.190
It was written a long time ago.

00:19:49.190 --> 00:19:50.850
Yeah, you're right.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:54.130
Miura only came this year, 
so he couldn't have done it.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.320
It's probably been here a long time.

00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:00.930
Maybe someone who already graduated wrote it.

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:03.550
B-But...

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:07.440
That ghost story only started 
to spread recently, didn't it?

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:08.680
Why is that?

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:14.990
<i>Someone with an uncontrollable 
hatred for women</i>

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:18.190
<i>probably drew these scribbles.</i>

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:20.070
<i>Little by little,</i>

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:22.730
<i>those feelings collected 
here, like a landfill.</i>

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:26.720
<i>Negative emotions kept building up.</i>

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:31.850
<i>But eventually, won't the 
landfill run out of space?</i>

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:35.790
<i>This feeling... This weird feeling...</i>

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:36.910
<i>What is it?</i>

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:39.820
<i>I'm on the verge of learning 
something, but...</i>

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:45.090
Tashiro!

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:46.720
Inaba!

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:51.130
What are you people doing here?

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:53.560
M-Miura...

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.840
No, let me go.

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:58.910
What are you people doing here?!

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:01.410
<i>Those eyes again!</i>

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:04.810
We aren't doing anything.

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:05.480
Liar!

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:06.860
I'm not a liar!

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:07.970
Liar!

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:10.150
Liar! Liar! Liar! Liar!

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:11.790
Listen to us...

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:13.590
Just release Tashiro—

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:16.580
What is this?

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:18.700
Is it coming from those scribbles?

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:25.890
Girls... Die.

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:29.800
Girls... Die...

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:34.060
Girls! Die!

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:34.060
Stop it!

00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:12.330
What happened?

00:23:12.330 --> 00:23:14.930
What happened to Miura? To JTB?

00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:16.610
What is this "muddy feeling"?

00:23:16.610 --> 00:23:19.540
Even with the power of the three Norns...

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:20.950
We don't know!

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:24.480
Forget that. I will never 
dress like that again.

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:26.380
Got it? Never!

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:28.370
Is that foreshadowing?

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:31.790
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:33.180
<b>Eleventh Haunting 
The Worst Possible Meeting</b>

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:32.930
The Worst Possible Meeting.

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:36.300
All the keys are hidden in that tiny room?
